description.p:
Suitable further substituents, which are optional, for the ortho-substituted phenyl ring include 

 for example methylthio or ethylthio; Ci^alkylsulfmyl for example methylsulfmyl, ethylsulfinyl or propylsulfinyl; Cι-6alkylsulfonyl for example methylsulfonyl or ethylsulfonyl; Ci^alkoxy for example methoxy, ethoxy or propoxy; halo for example bromo, fluoro, chloro or iodo; carboxy; Cι-6alkoxycarbonyl for example methoxycarbonyl; 

 for example acetyl or propionyl; nitro; amino; C]-6alkylamino for example methylamino or ethylamino; di-Ci-6alkylamino where the alkyl groups may be the same or different, for example dimethylamino; trifluoromethyl; CF3S(O)x wherein x is 0 to 2, for example trifluoromethylthio, trifluoromethylsulfinyl or trifiuoromethylsulfonyl; C]-6alkanoylamino for example acetylamino or propionylamino; Cι-6alkylsulphonamido for example methylsulphonamido; ureido; Cι-6alkylureido for example methylureido (MeNHCONH-), di-C1-6alkylureido for example dimethylureido (Me2NCONH-); carbamoyl; C1-6alkylcarbamoyl for example methylcarbamoyl; 

 where the alkyl groups may be the same or different, for example dimethylcarbamoyl; and Cι-6alkyl for example methyl substituted by any ofthe hereinabove substituents. Another suitable further substituent for the ortho-substituted ring is hydroxy.

